  "theme": "ivory-lace-pearls",
  "note": "G157 recolour manifest (tools/recolor_parts.py, docs/25). Two families share the ivory hue and are told apart by chroma: lace (lace, roses, satin bow, petal; chroma >= .025) and satin (the painted satin ground and mist; groups satin only). A palette either tints the lace (blush, champagne, mauve) or keeps it ivory on a tinted satin ground (dusty blue, sage). The antique gold brooch and pearl drop never change; photo placeholders stay ivory. leaf = the green of the baby's breath sprigs (always kept); scene_satin = the satin of the share image, tinted only with tinted lace (an ivory-lace palette keeps the share image ivory so its roses stay ivory).",
